# Lapila stdlib: ErasedCallable, a routine value whose signature is known only at run time

module System

### A routine value whose signature is known only at run time: the routine's address, its kind (a routine that gives
### its value directly, or one that gives the carrier of a failable call) and a hash of its signature (its parameter
### and result types, each with its module, the same number `typeid` gives the Callable type). Routine values of
### different signatures fit in one place (`List[ErasedCallable]`). `f.to[ErasedCallable]()` makes one of a routine
### or a Callable value, and `e.to[Callable[(S64,), S64]]()` gives the routine value back when the signatures match.
### The value it gives back may give any failure the program throws, as a Callable kept in a field does.
record ErasedCallable
    ### The routine's address.
    secret entry: Addr
    ### 0 for a routine that gives its value directly, 1 for one that gives the carrier of a failable call.
    secret kind: U8
    ### The signature hash.
    secret signature: U64

### A routine value that an `ErasedCallable` was asked for as another routine type than its own.
crashable RoutineSignatureError
    ### The routine type that was asked for.
    asked: @[Byte]

### Writes `The erased routine value is not a Callable[(S64,), S64].`
### :typeparam TWriter: The type of the Writer.
### :param out: The Writer the message goes to.
routine RoutineSignatureError.message_into[TWriter](out: @TWriter) -> None
needs TWriter obeys Writer
    out.write("The erased routine value is not a {me.asked}.")
    return

### Gives the routine value back as the routine type `T` it was made from. A call through it may give any failure the
### program throws.
### :typeparam T: The routine type, `Callable[(S64,), S64]`.
### :returns: The routine value.
### :throws: {RoutineSignatureError} when the routine value has another signature than `T`.
routine ErasedCallable.to[T]() -> T
needs AnyType T
    if me.signature != typeid[T]()
        throw RoutineSignatureError(asked: type_name[T]())
    return open_callable[T](entry: me.entry, kind: me.kind)

### Whether the routine value has the signature of the routine type `T`.
### :typeparam T: The routine type, `Callable[(S64,), S64]`.
### :returns: `true` when `to[T]()` gives it back.
routine ErasedCallable.fits[T]() -> Bool
needs AnyType T
    return me.signature == typeid[T]()
